      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Find $k$ if $2$ is a root of $f(x)={x}^{4}+k{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-57x+6k.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=2$ is a root, we have $f(2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{4}+k(2)^{3}-7(2)^{2}-57(2)+6k & =0 \\\\ 16+8k-28-114+6k & =0 \\\\ 14k-126 & =0 \\\\ 14k & =126 \\\\ k & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
